  "text" : "An agent harnesses everything except the model.\nIt decides what the model sees, what it can do, what it remembers, and when it's done.\nContext is what goes into the model on this turn.\nIt's your instructions, the files that opened the last error, tools are what it can touch.\nRead a file, run a command, search the web.\nMemory is what carries over when the session ends.\nNotes, rules, like an agent's MD, they're loaded back in next time.\nAnd the loop runs the model, runs the tool, feeds the result back, and checks the work.\nTry again or stop, and it can even save rules to recursively self-improve.\nThe model can be the same, but the harness is why one agent fixes your bug and another\nmight keep going in circles.\nSo when your agent fails, don't blame the model at first.\nAsk which piece was missing—the context, the tool, the memory, or the check."
}
